1
00:00:40,248 --> 00:00:41,875
<i>They are currently in our custody.</i>

2
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:45,462
<i>Their lawyers are appealing</i>
<i>for mitigating circumstances,</i>

3
00:00:45,545 --> 00:00:46,379
<i>arguing that, in the end,</i>

4
00:00:46,463 --> 00:00:49,674
<i>they helped dismantle</i>
<i>the Concordat and La Morte Bianca.</i>

5
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:54,387
Maybe she just turned your adventure
business into a real adventure?

6
00:00:54,471 --> 00:00:56,890
<i>Mikoy, I have no problem with adventure.</i>

7
00:00:56,973 --> 00:00:58,183
But Chiara is different.

8
00:00:58,266 --> 00:00:59,768
Whenever I take her as my tour guide,

9
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:01,519
I feel like I'm in
a permanent danger zone!

10
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:05,523
<i>I thought you wanted to know what</i>
<i>really happened to Mikoy and Chiara.</i>

11
00:01:08,026 --> 00:01:09,486
<i>Look how big it is!</i>

12
00:01:09,569 --> 00:01:11,696
<i>So, assuming you catch</i>
<i>a fish in the river…</i>

13
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:13,073
<i>Like sashimi, like in Japan.</i>

14
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:15,033
- <i>Rhamboy.</i>
- <i>Right?</i>

15
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:16,367
- <i>What are you doing?</i>
- <i>Aunt Tess.</i>

16
00:01:16,451 --> 00:01:17,827
<i>I'm vlogging.</i>

17
00:01:17,911 --> 00:01:20,914
<i>What are you doing</i>
<i>with that enormous fish?</i>

18
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:35,428
At least I'm not boring!

19
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:38,014
You need something new every now and then.

20
00:01:38,097 --> 00:01:40,141
Not something boring,
not something that's always the same.

21
00:01:49,109 --> 00:01:51,820
Wait. Why Albay?

22
00:01:58,451 --> 00:02:02,539
Plus, their food is so good.

23
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:04,332
You know, laing,

24
00:02:04,415 --> 00:02:05,500
- inangat.
- Inangat.

25
00:02:05,583 --> 00:02:07,001
- Inangat!
- Inangat!

26
00:02:08,419 --> 00:02:09,587
- Yummy!
- Wow!

27
00:02:09,671 --> 00:02:12,382
You two are really in sync, huh.
Did you practice that?

28
00:02:13,591 --> 00:02:14,968
- Hungry.
- We're just hungry.

29
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:17,011
You two!

30
00:02:24,435 --> 00:02:26,729
He inherited a piece of land
from his parents.

31
00:02:27,438 --> 00:02:29,732
The only reason he's in Cebu
is because of Ma'am Tess.

32
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:33,194
But the truth is, he's a true-blue Oragon.

33
00:02:33,945 --> 00:02:38,158
And it's probably traumatic
for them to return to Cebu

34
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:39,951
after everything that happened.

35
00:02:40,034 --> 00:02:42,662
While in Bicol, his territory,

36
00:02:47,834 --> 00:02:51,129
What kind of future
would Mikoy have there?

37
00:03:03,600 --> 00:03:08,897
<i>Magayon! Don't be shy!</i>

38
00:03:08,980 --> 00:03:13,943
<i>Come out! My lovely goddess!</i>

39
00:03:14,027 --> 00:03:18,740
<i>Clear away the clouds</i>

40
00:03:18,823 --> 00:03:22,452
<i>My love!</i>

41
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:26,539
<i>Just give me</i>

42
00:03:26,623 --> 00:03:29,792
<i>That beautiful smile!</i>

43
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:41,346
<i>Magayon!</i>

44
00:03:41,429 --> 00:03:44,265
Okay, good morning, everyone! Welcome!

45
00:03:44,349 --> 00:03:49,270
Today, we'll show you
one of Bicol's greatest prides.

46
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:52,273
The art of abaca weaving!

47
00:03:52,357 --> 00:03:54,984
Because <i>iba ka</i>. You're different.

48
00:03:55,068 --> 00:03:56,819
There!

49
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:57,946
So, here we are.

50
00:03:58,029 --> 00:04:00,573
Most people think this is just a rope.

51
00:04:00,657 --> 00:04:03,034
But no, that is very, very wrong.

52
00:04:03,117 --> 00:04:08,373
This is where bags, mats, hats,
and wall art all begin.

53
00:04:08,456 --> 00:04:11,251
And sometimes, it's even
the cause of marital fights

54
00:04:11,334 --> 00:04:13,711
because they picked the wrong color…

55
00:04:15,088 --> 00:04:17,006
curtains!

56
00:04:17,090 --> 00:04:19,759
The fibers are extracted
from the abaca plant.

57
00:04:19,842 --> 00:04:22,720
Those are the plants you see behind us.

58
00:04:23,596 --> 00:04:24,430
See?

59
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:26,849
You thought they were
just banana trees, didn't you?

60
00:04:26,933 --> 00:04:27,934
But they're actually abaca plants.

61
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:33,147
But we're still not sure.
Because it's just <i>a-"baka"</i> maybe.

62
00:04:36,943 --> 00:04:39,487
After that, it's dried under the sun.

63
00:04:39,570 --> 00:04:44,367
Once it's dry,
it's cleaned, sorted, and graded

64
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:47,662
depending on its thickness and quality.

65
00:04:47,745 --> 00:04:49,038
It's just like a beauty pageant.

66
00:04:49,122 --> 00:04:52,709
Of course, there's
a first runner-up and a winner!

67
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,589
Of course, this is what it will look like.

68
00:04:58,673 --> 00:05:01,009
See? Isn't it beautiful?
It's also very soft.

69
00:05:01,092 --> 00:05:06,556
And that's not all.
It can also be made into fans.

70
00:05:06,639 --> 00:05:08,474
For sweaty people like me.

71
00:05:08,558 --> 00:05:12,186
And these are for you, too,
since you're all sweating now.

72
00:05:12,770 --> 00:05:15,148
Alright, ladies and gentlemen, finally!

73
00:05:15,231 --> 00:05:18,735
We've arrived at one
of Bicol's top products!

74
00:05:19,402 --> 00:05:20,737
Pili nuts!

75
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:22,613
The finest handpicked nuts!

76
00:05:22,697 --> 00:05:24,490
But before anything else,
we need to use this first,

77
00:05:24,574 --> 00:05:26,117
so we can get the…

78
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:29,037
the chosen heart.

79
00:05:30,913 --> 00:05:32,248
Who wants one?

80
00:05:41,424 --> 00:05:43,092
So, who wants one?

81
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:49,974
With his profile, we know that
even though he's just starting out,

82
00:05:50,058 --> 00:05:52,185
we know that with his resourcefulness,

83
00:05:52,268 --> 00:05:53,811
he'll be able to get back
on his feet quickly.

84
00:05:59,942 --> 00:06:01,903
Just like a universal charger.

85
00:06:01,986 --> 00:06:03,946
You're right! Correct!

86
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,198
Um…

87
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:19,337
Well, I think Mikoy and Chiara
are the happiest they've ever been.

88
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:25,802
<i>They've overcome</i>
<i>the biggest challenge of their lives.</i>

89
00:06:28,971 --> 00:06:33,226
<i>And now, they have the chance to live</i>
<i>a normal and happy life.</i>

90
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:37,271
<i>So I'm certain</i>
<i>that every moment of their lives,</i>

91
00:06:37,355 --> 00:06:40,108
<i>they'll be filled with happiness and love.</i>

92
00:06:48,741 --> 00:06:50,326
Wait, I have a feeling
something's going on.

93
00:06:50,409 --> 00:06:51,828
I'm a senator. Why am I standing?

94
00:06:53,037 --> 00:06:54,789
- Yes, sorry. My apologies.
- Get up from there.

95
00:07:20,106 --> 00:07:22,984
Dekyo! Ka Pepe! Come on, let's eat here!

96
00:07:23,067 --> 00:07:24,360
Hey, he said let's eat.

97
00:07:24,944 --> 00:07:26,446
It's okay. We're still working on a play.

98
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:28,531
We have a three-on-three later.

99
00:07:28,614 --> 00:07:29,615
Wow, impressive.

100
00:07:31,159 --> 00:07:32,118
You sure?

101
00:07:32,201 --> 00:07:33,161
We're good!

102
00:07:35,288 --> 00:07:37,957
<i>Is this idiot really angry?</i>

103
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:41,043
<i>Am I the one who should apologize to him?</i>

104
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:45,381
<i>If you don't want</i>
<i>to talk to me, then don't.</i>

105
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:47,842
Hey, stay here for a while! Let's chat!

106
00:07:48,843 --> 00:07:50,761
It's like they're different people now!

107
00:07:51,929 --> 00:07:54,599
Come on. Don't be shy.

108
00:07:57,602 --> 00:08:01,439
<i>And he's really talking</i>
<i>to someone else while I'm here.</i>

109
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:05,735
<i>I admit that I did something wrong.</i>

110
00:08:05,818 --> 00:08:07,945
<i>But for everything to be blamed on me…</i>

111
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:13,242
<i>Should I break his pinky</i>
<i>so he'll learn his lesson?</i>

112
00:08:18,748 --> 00:08:20,708
Do you want to have lunch later?

113
00:08:21,375 --> 00:08:22,418
No, it's okay.

114
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:23,961
Let's just meet after work.

115
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:28,257
Hey, come on!

116
00:08:29,050 --> 00:08:31,552
What are you doing there?
What kind of strategy is that?

117
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:34,597
This is the triangle offense.

118
00:08:35,223 --> 00:08:36,098
I know that!

119
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:42,897
Was what I did really that bad?

120
00:08:43,564 --> 00:08:45,566
I'm really getting annoyed with Mikoy.

121
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:47,985
You're the one giving me
the cold treatment?

122
00:08:48,528 --> 00:08:51,531
What if I dunked your head
in a bucket of ice?

123
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:54,534
So annoying.

124
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:57,453
He's getting on my nerves.
Fine, if that's what he wants--

125
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:02,124
You're back?

126
00:09:02,750 --> 00:09:04,252
Do you need something?

127
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:05,878
Nothing. Just my coffee.

128
00:09:05,962 --> 00:09:07,505
Because I enjoy having coffee
while using the bathroom.

129
00:09:08,297 --> 00:09:10,716
We'll talk later when I get home, okay?

130
00:09:10,800 --> 00:09:13,594
We'll have a long chat!

131
00:09:19,308 --> 00:09:21,727
Chiara, let's talk.

132
00:09:21,811 --> 00:09:22,812
I don't want to.

133
00:09:23,479 --> 00:09:24,689
You're dead!

134
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:31,821
Mom! Let's walk together.

135
00:09:34,574 --> 00:09:35,950
You, Mikoy.

136
00:09:36,576 --> 00:09:39,120
Why are you and Chiara
not going to work together?

137
00:09:39,203 --> 00:09:41,038
Why did she leave first?

138
00:09:43,082 --> 00:09:45,293
It's so early.

139
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:48,170
You're still denying it.

140
00:09:48,254 --> 00:09:50,256
I know you guys have a problem.

141
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:55,595
We had an argument yesterday.

142
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:56,512
Why?

143
00:09:57,680 --> 00:09:59,765
She's so stubborn.

144
00:09:59,849 --> 00:10:02,143
So irresponsible.

145
00:10:02,226 --> 00:10:05,730
She didn't even think that it's me
who recommended her to Sir Pandoy.

146
00:10:05,813 --> 00:10:07,648
I feel responsible.

147
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:10,026
I'll be embarrassed.

148
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:15,364
Have you guys talked about why
she's acting like that?

149
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:20,828
Our voices started to rise as we argued.

150
00:10:20,911 --> 00:10:23,581
How about earlier, was her tone the same?

151
00:10:24,832 --> 00:10:25,666
See?

152
00:10:27,126 --> 00:10:29,170
See? I knew it.

153
00:10:29,253 --> 00:10:30,963
You're sulking too much.

154
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:33,466
You could've solved it earlier.

155
00:10:33,549 --> 00:10:36,302
Of course, I'm still annoyed.

156
00:10:36,886 --> 00:10:39,513
Is this not the life we imagined?

157
00:10:39,597 --> 00:10:42,933
Now, it seems like
she's sabotaging everything.

158
00:10:44,852 --> 00:10:48,481
Is she giving up?
She doesn't want this anymore?

159
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:51,817
Is this life too simple for her?

160
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:58,532
Son, instead of telling me that,

161
00:10:58,616 --> 00:11:00,368
why don't you talk to her?

162
00:11:39,323 --> 00:11:41,534
<i>Is he still not talking to you?</i>

163
00:11:42,284 --> 00:11:44,120
<i>Still ignoring you?</i>

164
00:11:47,123 --> 00:11:51,335
Yes, and this is actually
our longest fight ever.

165
00:11:51,419 --> 00:11:55,214
Usually, we don't sleep
until we've sorted things out.

166
00:11:55,881 --> 00:11:59,927
What did you tell him?
And what exactly did you guys fight about?

167
00:12:01,345 --> 00:12:02,888
Not much.

168
00:12:02,972 --> 00:12:05,057
What do you mean "not much"?!

169
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:07,726
Mikoy of all people?

170
00:12:08,394 --> 00:12:11,856
<i>Get angry over nothing?</i>
<i>Giving you the cold shoulder over nothing?</i>

171
00:12:14,191 --> 00:12:18,737
Well, I said I'm not a boring person.

172
00:12:18,821 --> 00:12:20,781
<i>Dear, tell me the whole story.</i>

173
00:12:20,865 --> 00:12:25,995
Give me all the details
if you want advice from me.

174
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:31,542
Not just half of the information.

175
00:12:31,625 --> 00:12:34,545
If that's the case,
then just call on the radio.

176
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:39,633
Well, there's a…

177
00:12:40,384 --> 00:12:42,011
problem at work.

178
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:45,347
I became a little stubborn.

179
00:12:45,431 --> 00:12:46,390
A little bit.

180
00:12:46,974 --> 00:12:47,892
A little bit?

181
00:12:48,809 --> 00:12:52,021
It's Mikoy who recommended me
for this job.

182
00:12:52,104 --> 00:12:54,398
Why did you have to act up?

183
00:12:55,566 --> 00:12:56,775
Maybe because I'm bored.

184
00:12:58,986 --> 00:13:00,654
Are you sure you're just bored?

185
00:13:02,364 --> 00:13:04,825
Wow, in fairness to this…

186
00:13:05,784 --> 00:13:07,786
smuggled phone,

187
00:13:07,870 --> 00:13:13,000
the quality is really good.
I can feel the depth of your sigh.

188
00:13:13,083 --> 00:13:16,879
Your sigh that's as deep
as the Pacific Ocean.

189
00:13:16,962 --> 00:13:21,050
Okay, if not because of being bored,
maybe because I feel like I'm stuck.

190
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:24,970
There you go!

191
00:13:25,054 --> 00:13:26,972
I'm happy.

192
00:13:28,807 --> 00:13:29,808
It's just…

193
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:32,770
He seems like he doesn't have a plan.

194
00:13:34,355 --> 00:13:35,814
Plan about what?

195
00:14:00,422 --> 00:14:03,801
You have to understand Chiara's situation.

196
00:14:04,301 --> 00:14:06,428
Her parents are in prison.

197
00:14:07,638 --> 00:14:11,934
Think about the frustration
of being alone without your family.

198
00:14:12,017 --> 00:14:13,269
No siblings.

199
00:14:14,103 --> 00:14:15,062
Just alone.

200
00:14:17,189 --> 00:14:18,357
But I'm here.

201
00:14:20,109 --> 00:14:21,569
I know,

202
00:14:21,652 --> 00:14:26,198
but it's inevitable for her to feel

203
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:29,952
that she's alone in this new life.

204
00:14:30,035 --> 00:14:33,289
A fresh and new life
with only the two of you.

205
00:14:33,372 --> 00:14:36,000
Son, here's the question.

206
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:40,796
What will you do to reassure her?

207
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:41,714
Right?

208
00:14:41,797 --> 00:14:44,133
What decision will you make

209
00:14:44,216 --> 00:14:46,427
for her to not feel lonely?

210
00:14:46,927 --> 00:14:50,055
So that you two are a real family.

211
00:15:03,277 --> 00:15:06,405
There! Smile!

212
00:15:06,989 --> 00:15:07,823
Pose like this!

213
00:15:14,955 --> 00:15:17,333
Your pictures are so cute!

214
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:22,171
I'll just get off, please.

215
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:23,923
It's so scary.

216
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:26,091
No, you can do it!

217
00:15:26,175 --> 00:15:29,720
I believe in you.
You have to believe in yourself too.

218
00:15:29,803 --> 00:15:34,183
I won't invalidate
that feeling of yours because it's real.

219
00:15:34,266 --> 00:15:37,144
Your feelings are real.
You just have to overcome it

220
00:15:37,227 --> 00:15:39,563
- Okay.
- and embrace it.

221
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:41,690
- Okay? You can do it.
- Okay.

222
00:15:41,774 --> 00:15:44,318
- We'll count together, okay?
- Okay.

223
00:15:44,401 --> 00:15:46,111
- On three.
- Slowly, okay?

224
00:15:54,411 --> 00:15:56,789
I told you, you can do it!

225
00:16:05,214 --> 00:16:07,716
Water? Or do you want to take a rest?

226
00:16:07,800 --> 00:16:12,179
It's okay. We might be late
and miss the sunset.

227
00:16:12,262 --> 00:16:16,058
It's fine. I have an idea
so we can go faster.

228
00:16:16,141 --> 00:16:18,727
Oh no, it's okay. It's really okay.

229
00:16:18,811 --> 00:16:21,689
- It's alright, so we can go faster.
- Are you sure?

230
00:16:21,772 --> 00:16:23,983
- Yes, no worries.
- Thank you!

231
00:16:24,692 --> 00:16:27,528
- Thank you!
- Okay, watch your step.

232
00:16:27,611 --> 00:16:29,446
It's a little slippery over here.

233
00:16:34,868 --> 00:16:36,286
Yes, sir.

234
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:40,666
The lunch are prepared for the ATV guests.

235
00:16:40,749 --> 00:16:41,792
Yes, Sir Pandoy.

236
00:16:41,875 --> 00:16:43,794
Yes, sir. I'm expecting it already.

237
00:16:43,877 --> 00:16:45,004
Yes.

238
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:46,130
Goodbye.

239
00:16:48,298 --> 00:16:50,509
- Ma'am Den. Ma'am Den.
- Yes, Mikoy?

240
00:16:50,592 --> 00:16:53,387
Can I talk to Sir Pandoy?

241
00:16:53,470 --> 00:16:56,432
We weren't able to talk last time.

242
00:16:56,515 --> 00:16:59,059
I want to say sorry on behalf of Chiara.

243
00:16:59,143 --> 00:17:05,315
You know, she's from Prague
and has family problems.

244
00:17:06,692 --> 00:17:08,402
What are you talking about?

245
00:17:08,485 --> 00:17:11,405
They already talked earlier.

246
00:17:14,283 --> 00:17:17,953
- Sir! Sir Pandoy, can we talk?
- Chiara.

247
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:19,079
About what?

248
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:23,917
<i>Yes! Chiara went there</i>
<i>and asked for forgiveness.</i>

249
00:17:24,001 --> 00:17:26,086
And she was given another chance.

250
00:17:27,004 --> 00:17:27,838
Really?!

251
00:17:30,466 --> 00:17:31,300
Huh?

252
00:17:32,426 --> 00:17:34,136
Is Sir Pandoy sure?

253
00:17:35,137 --> 00:17:37,097
You said it yourself,

254
00:17:37,181 --> 00:17:39,725
it's her first time in this kind of life.

255
00:17:39,808 --> 00:17:41,852
She might get bored, right?

256
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:46,982
I also told her
that if she has any suggestions

257
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:50,569
that is good for the ATV, she can tell me.

258
00:17:50,652 --> 00:17:52,529
We are open to any changes.

259
00:17:53,614 --> 00:17:56,325
You know, I'm impressed by Chiara.

260
00:17:56,408 --> 00:17:59,787
I'm sure she'll go a long way
in this business.

261
00:18:01,371 --> 00:18:04,458
Thank you, ma'am.
I'll personally thank Sir Pandoy

262
00:18:04,541 --> 00:18:06,502
for giving Chiara a second chance.

263
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:12,424
Except Hitler.

264
00:18:13,634 --> 00:18:14,760
Makes sense!

265
00:18:14,843 --> 00:18:16,345
Okay, I'll go ahead.

266
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:17,971
- Okay.
- Sir might scold me.

267
00:18:18,055 --> 00:18:20,015
- Bye!
- Take care.

268
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:38,617
I have good news.

269
00:18:39,910 --> 00:18:40,744
Chiara.

270
00:18:42,329 --> 00:18:43,163
The thing is…

271
00:18:44,164 --> 00:18:45,332
Something happened to Mikoy.

272
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:46,959
What is it?

273
00:18:47,042 --> 00:18:49,962
He's in the ecopark,
at the top of the mountain.

274
00:18:52,798 --> 00:18:54,633
- Chiara…
- Chiara!

275
00:18:55,509 --> 00:18:56,385
Chiara!

276
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:06,145
I'm coming, Mikoy.

277
00:19:07,521 --> 00:19:09,356
What is happening to you?

278
00:19:40,762 --> 00:19:41,597
Mikoy!

279
00:19:43,515 --> 00:19:44,641
Mikoy!

280
00:19:48,812 --> 00:19:49,646
Mikoy!

281
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:58,864
Mikoy!

282
00:20:09,458 --> 00:20:10,334
Mikoy?

283
00:20:14,630 --> 00:20:15,756
Mikoy!

284
00:20:16,757 --> 00:20:17,674
Mikoy!

285
00:20:25,724 --> 00:20:26,600
Mikoy.

286
00:20:32,064 --> 00:20:34,733
Mikoy, are you okay?

287
00:20:34,816 --> 00:20:37,361
What is this for? What happened?

288
00:20:44,076 --> 00:20:45,911
I'm not good with words.

289
00:20:49,748 --> 00:20:50,791
All I know is that

290
00:20:51,917 --> 00:20:54,962
this story started
when I was searching for something.

291
00:21:00,801 --> 00:21:03,720
Searching for an opportunity
to help my family.

292
00:21:05,514 --> 00:21:06,807
For a better life.

293
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:11,353
An opportunity to leave poverty behind.

294
00:21:18,735 --> 00:21:20,279
Then I met you.

295
00:21:27,494 --> 00:21:28,537
Unbelievable!

296
00:21:30,122 --> 00:21:31,039
Too beautiful.

297
00:21:34,334 --> 00:21:35,627
Too wealthy.

298
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:45,345
And worst of all,

299
00:21:46,013 --> 00:21:47,556
the daughter of a mafia boss.

300
00:21:56,481 --> 00:21:57,733
So many secrets,

301
00:22:00,819 --> 00:22:02,195
things to hide.

302
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:07,784
You know what?

303
00:22:08,910 --> 00:22:10,287
If I gambled,

304
00:22:11,413 --> 00:22:15,208
I never would've bet on us surviving
all that we've been through.

305
00:22:24,176 --> 00:22:26,219
even if we just stare out the window,

306
00:22:26,762 --> 00:22:28,388
being bored.

307
00:22:29,848 --> 00:22:32,893
I don't even care
if we have to jump out of a helicopter

308
00:22:32,976 --> 00:22:35,062
or in the river.

309
00:22:38,648 --> 00:22:40,859
I don't care if a bomb hits me right now.

310
00:22:43,653 --> 00:22:47,532
It doesn't matter if the whole world
is mad at you.

311
00:22:53,080 --> 00:22:54,998
I will face them all for you.

312
00:23:09,471 --> 00:23:12,724
Ms. Chiara Valtrovi.

313
00:23:20,398 --> 00:23:22,192
You are my greatest adventure.

314
00:23:26,905 --> 00:23:28,615
And the greatest love of my life.

315
00:23:38,875 --> 00:23:40,460
You are the real Pinagpala.

316
00:24:25,630 --> 00:24:28,675
Mr. Mikoy Pinagpala, I will marry you.

317
00:24:28,758 --> 00:24:34,264
I will be with you until my last breath.

318
00:26:02,519 --> 00:26:06,690
That's why I'm so grateful
for accepting me.

319
00:26:19,077 --> 00:26:22,747
<i>But I don't think they would love</i>
<i>to go back and serve the agency.</i>

320
00:26:22,831 --> 00:26:26,793
We can convince them.
We can use Chiara's parents.

321
00:26:26,876 --> 00:26:33,091
In exchange, we can release the people
that are important to Chiara.

322
00:26:34,801 --> 00:26:37,095
<i>Seriously, are you really going on a date?</i>

323
00:26:37,178 --> 00:26:39,597
Who is this? A person
you matched with online?

324
00:26:39,681 --> 00:26:42,726
Bok, to be honest,

325
00:26:47,647 --> 00:26:49,899
Wait, who is it? Do I know the person?

326
00:26:53,653 --> 00:26:54,821
Agent Alex!

327
00:26:54,904 --> 00:26:55,822
How are you?

328
00:26:55,905 --> 00:26:56,823
<i>Is there a problem?</i>

329
00:26:56,906 --> 00:26:58,408
You miss me, don't you?

330
00:26:58,491 --> 00:26:59,868
<i>Agent Alex!</i>

331
00:26:59,951 --> 00:27:02,329
Right, why did you call?

332
00:27:02,412 --> 00:27:04,622
I just wanted to tell you that…
